level_guide_text = "[center][b][u]LEVEL 2: PRECISION & CHARACTERS[/u][/b][/center]

[b]OBJECTIVE:[/b]
Not all numbers are integers! Differentiate between single characters and different types of decimals.

[b]THEORY GUIDE:[/b]

[b]1. FLOAT (float)[/b]
Used for simple decimals. In code, they often end with an 'f'.
[i]Example:[/i] [code]float speed = 9.8f;[/code]

[b]2. DOUBLE (double)[/b]
Used for very precise or large decimal numbers.
[i]Example:[/i] [code]double price = 19.99;[/code]

[b]3. CHAR (char)[/b]
Stores a [color=#fab005]single letter[/color] or symbol. Unlike Strings, these use [color=#fab005]'single quotes'[/color].
[i]Example:[/i] [code]char grade = 'B';[/code]"

